<Layout title="Drylining Edinburgh | Partition Walls &amp; Ceilings Contractors" description="Professional drylining contractors in Edinburgh. Expert partition walls, suspended ceilings, and plasterboard installation for the New Town, Old Town, Leith Waterfront, and the wider EH1–EH36 postcode region. Free quotes." canonical="/areas/edinburgh/" schema={schema}>
  <section style="position:relative;min-height:400px;display:flex;align-items:center;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#1a1a2e 0%,#16213e 100%);overflow:hidden;"> <img src="/images/hero-main.jpg" alt="Drylining services in Edinburgh's New Town and Old Town" style="position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;opacity:0.25;"> <div class="container" style="position:relative;z-index:1;text-align:center;padding:60px 20px;"> <nav style="font-size:13px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.70);margin-bottom:12px;"> <a href="/" style="text-decoration:none;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.70);">Home</a> / <a href="/areas/" style="text-decoration:none;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.70);">Areas</a> / <span style="color:#ffffff;">Drylining in Edinburgh</span> </nav> <h1 style="font-size:clamp(28px,4vw,44px);font-weight:800;color:#ffffff;margin-bottom:14px;line-height:1.15;">Drylining in Edinburgh</h1> <p style="font-size:17px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.85);max-width:700px;margin:0 auto;line-height:1.6;">CSCS-accredited drylining contractors delivering partition walls, suspended ceilings, and plasterboard across Edinburgh city centre, the New Town, Old Town, Leith Waterfront, and the wider EH1–EH36 postcode region.</p> </div> </section> <section class="section"><div class="container" style="max-width:900px;"> <div style="padding:24px;margin-bottom:24px;border-left:4px solid var(--primary);background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);"> <p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;color:var(--text);"><strong>TL;DR:</strong> Drylining Edinburgh provides drylining, partition walls, and suspended ceilings across Edinburgh (EH1–EH36), Leith, and the entire City of Edinburgh council area. Experienced with Victorian sandstone tenements, New Town Georgian properties, and major regeneration projects including Sighthill and Fountainbridge.</p> </div> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Drylining Services in Edinburgh</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Edinburgh is Scotland's capital city with a population of over 540,000 people across the EH1–EH36 postcode areas. Home to the UNESCO World Heritage Old Town and New Town, the Scottish Parliament, and one of the UK's most recognisable skylines dominated by Edinburgh Castle, the city offers an extraordinary mix of 16th-century sandstone tenements, Georgian grandeur on George Street, and modern developments at Leith Waterfront. This diversity means our drylining contractors work on everything from listed building interior renewals near the Royal Mile to large-scale student accommodation and commercial fit-outs along the Fountainbridge and Sighthill corridors.</p> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">The city's ongoing regeneration — including the NCC Engine Shed at Fort Kinnaird, the Sighthill regeneration programme, the Fountainbridge business quarter expansion, and hundreds of new build student accommodation blocks across the EH postcodes — creates consistent demand for commercial drylining services. We deliver partition wall installation, suspended ceilings, and fire-rated wall systems for student residences, hotels, office refurbishments, retail units, and healthcare premises throughout the City of Edinburgh. All work is carried out to Scottish Building Standards compliant with Sections 2 (Fire), 3 (Energy), and 4 (Sound).</p> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">What We Do in Edinburgh</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Our Edinburgh crew handles everything from single-room domestic renovations in Morningside to large-scale commercial fit-outs in the Financial District at St James — covering partition walls, suspended ceilings, and fire-rated wall systems across the entire EH1–EH36 postcode region.</p> <ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;"> <li><strong>Scottish tenement drylining</strong> — Internal wall insulation, room conversions, and partition walls in Victorian sandstone tenements and Georgian townhouses across the New Town, Old Town, Stockbridge, and Bruntsfield</li> <li><strong>Student accommodation drylining</strong> — Pre-completion drylining for student housing developments across the EH postcodes, including fire-rated compartmentation and acoustic party walls</li> <li><strong>Commercial fit-outs</strong> — Office refurbs, retail units, and hospitality venues along Princes Street, George Street, St James, and Leith Waterfront</li> <li><strong>Fire-rated walls</strong> — Multi-storey residential, student, and commercial buildings require Scottish Building Standards Section 2 (Fire) compliance, delivered with full documentation for City of Edinburgh Council building standards</li> <li><strong>Suspended ceilings</strong> — Office refurbs, healthcare premises, education facilities, and hospitality venues throughout the EH postcode area</li> <li><strong>Acoustic partitions</strong> — Tenement flats sharing party walls, student accommodation, and hotel conversions across the EH1–EH36 region</li> </ul> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Areas of Edinburgh We Cover</h2> <ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;"> <li>Edinburgh city centre (EH1) — Princes Street, Royal Mile, George Street, St James</li> <li>New Town (EH2) — Charlotte Square, Inverness Street, Rose Street</li> <li>Old Town (EH1) — Royal Mile, Canongate, Cowgate, Grassmarket</li> <li>Leith (EH6) — Leith Walk, Waterfront, Shore, Great Junction Street</li> <li>Stockbridge (EH3) — Dean Garden, Castle Terrace, Inverleith Park</li> <li>Morningside (EH10) — Morningside Road, Comiston Road, Bruntsfield Links</li> <li>Bruntsfield &amp; Marchmont (EH10) — Haymarket Terrace, Marionville Road</li> <li>Fountainbridge &amp; Clermiston (EH3/EH9) — Fountainbridge, Clermiston</li> <li>Sighthill &amp; Gorgie (EH11) — Saughton Bridge, Gorgie Road</li> <li>Ingliston &amp; Sighthill (EH28) — Business parks, retail parks, industrial estates</li> </ul> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Edinburgh Building Regulations &amp; Planning</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Edinburgh falls under <strong>City of Edinburgh Council</strong> for building standards and planning. The city contains an extraordinary concentration of protected buildings — over 4,500 listed buildings, 8 conservation areas, and two UNESCO World Heritage Sites (the Old Town and New Town). Many properties are within the <strong>New Town Conservation Area</strong> or <strong>Old Town Conservation Area</strong>, meaning internal structural alterations in listed buildings require listed building consent from the council. We work closely with clients, architects, and the council's building standards department to ensure every project — from a simple room partition in a Georgian house on Inverleith Row to a large-scale commercial fit-out at Fort Kinnaird — is fully compliant with Scottish Building Standards and any additional conservation requirements.</p> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Why Choose Us for Edinburgh Projects</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">As an Edinburgh-based drylining team with daily operations across the city and wider Lothians, we understand the unique demands of working in Scotland's capital. From navigating the narrow closes and closes of the Old Town to managing traffic restrictions in the New Town and working within the strict conservation guidelines of listed buildings, our crew knows Edinburgh inside out. We are familiar with Scottish Building Standards, hold all necessary Scottish construction accreditations, and understand the specific requirements of the city's diverse property stock — from 500-year-old sandstone tenements to cutting-edge new builds at Leith Waterfront.</p> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Related Services</h2> <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(180px,1fr));gap:10px;margin-bottom:1.5rem;"> <a href="/services/partition-walls/" style="text-decoration:none;padding:10px 14px;background:var(--white);border-radius:6px;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text);">Partition Walls</a> <a href="/services/fire-rated-drylining/" style="text-decoration:none;padding:10px 14px;background:var(--white);border-radius:6px;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text);">Fire-Rated Drylining</a> <a href="/services/acoustic-drylining/" style="text-decoration:none;padding:10px 14px;background:var(--white);border-radius:6px;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text);">Acoustic Drylining</a> <a href="/services/refurbishment-drylining/" style="text-decoration:none;padding:10px 14px;background:var(--white);border-radius:6px;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text);">Refurbishment Drylining</a> </div> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Nearby Areas</h2> <ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;"> <li><a href="/areas/leith/" style="color:var(--primary);text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;">Leith</a> — 5 minutes via A8</li> <li><a href="/areas/musselburgh/" style="color:var(--primary);text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;">Musselburgh</a> — 15 minutes via A1</li> <li><a href="/areas/dalkeith/" style="color:var(--primary);text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;">Dalkeith</a> — 15 minutes via A702</li> <li><a href="/areas/livingston/" style="color:var(--primary);text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;">Livingston</a> — 30 minutes via M8</li> </ul> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Get a Free Edinburgh Quote</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:2rem;">We offer free, no-obligation site visits and written quotes for all drylining projects across Edinburgh. Call us or fill in our quick form.</p> <div style="margin-top:2rem;text-align:center;"> <a href="/get-quote/" class="btn btn-primary" style="font-size:1.0625rem;padding:1rem 2.5rem;">Get a Free Edinburgh Quote</a> <a href="tel:08008203090" class="btn btn-secondary" style="font-size:1.0625rem;padding:1rem 2.5rem;border:2px solid var(--primary);background:transparent;color:var(--primary);margin-left:0.5rem;">FREEPHONE 0800 820 3090</a> </div> </div></section>  
</Layout>